./working_notes/promising_directions.md:207:The most promising positive route is a dyadic dual-localization theorem: failure of a fixed sublinear envelope should produce, for arbitrarily large \(n\), a dual certificate concentrated on horizons comparable to \(n\), hence \(D_n=\Omega(n)\). This is unproved and should first be tested in finite price alphabets and the formal left-limit model.
