./working_notes/literature_map.md:18:- Bistritz, Zhou, Chen, Bambos, and Blanchet (JMLR 2022), "No Weighted-Regret Learning in Adversarial Bandits with Delays," is verified. It studies delayed adversarial bandits with weighted-regret objectives and bounds involving total delay; relevant background for horizon-weighted finite-prefix dual certificates, not a delayed-fill characterization theorem.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:70:- Lagziel and Lehrer (Journal of Economic Theory 2015), "Approachability with delayed information," is verified. It gives delayed-information approachability/no-regret background and is relevant to vector-deficit formulations of simultaneous-horizon constraints; it does not prove the known-path finite-prefix LP or compactness criterion.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:83:- Bernstein and Shimkin (JMLR 2015) is verified. Response-based approachability may be algorithmically relevant if finite-prefix dual constraints are recast as vector-deficit feasibility; no direct delayed-fill result.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:84:- Dann, Mansour, Mohri, Schneider, and Sivan (COLT/PMLR 2025) is verified. It discusses rate-preserving reductions between approachability and generalized regret; relevant background for any future approachability formulation, not proof support for \(D_n\)-gluing.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:87:- Renault (Journal of Dynamics and Games 2014), "General limit value in dynamic programming," is verified. It gives a total-boundedness criterion for uniform convergence of values under vanishing-impatience evaluations. Relevant as uniform-value/gluing background only; it is not a theorem about delayed market making or \(D_n\).
./working_notes/literature_map.md:135:Iteration 12 adds internal exact finite-prefix machinery for deterministic known exogenous paths: the marginal reduction, finite-prefix LP dual \(D_n(P)\), and fixed-envelope compactness criterion. Literature checks found no direct theorem for this delayed-fill characterization. Lagziel-Lehrer 2015 is relevant delayed-approachability background for future vector-deficit formulations; Bistritz et al. 2022 is relevant weighted-regret delayed-bandit background for horizon-weighted certificates; Xie-Zhu-Shishkin 2025 is adjacent pricing context. All three should be cited as background only.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:137:Iteration 13 found no external theorem proving \(D_n=o(n)\Rightarrow o(T)\), nor a known market-path separator from the fixed-envelope criterion. The added approachability and uniform-value sources are background for possible formulations and for gluing cautions. Current internal proof work should focus on the last-exceedance/finite-prefix dual structure rather than importing uniform-value theorems wholesale.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:139:Iteration 14 found no direct external theorem proving gluing or a separator. The internal progress is an exact separated-block value, an exact dual boundary identity, and a finite-alphabet dual reduction. Fulkerson-Gross supports the interval-incidence vocabulary for the finite-alphabet formula, Renault 2014 and existing uniform-value sources reinforce the need for stability beyond scalar finite-prefix values, and pseudonorm/approachability and countably-infinite LP sources are possible formulation tools only.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:141:Iteration 15 found no external theorem for two-level gluing. The new fixed-design, infinite-game, dynamically changing environment, ordering, predictable-sequence, and Lindley-queue sources provide terminology or proof analogies for path-known regret, best-response formulations, process complexity, predictable paths, and reflected debt recursions. They should not be cited as proof support for CL-044, CL-045, or any \(D_n=o(n)\Rightarrow o(T)\) implication.
./working_notes/literature_map.md:143:Iteration 16 found no external theorem for the post-low or multi-low drought identities. The added Heliou-Mertikopoulos-Zhou delayed-reward paper is algorithmic background for continuous delayed payoff feedback. The Cao-Siska-Szpruch-Treetanthiploet and Albers-Cucuringu-Howison-Shestopaloff papers are adjacent market-making context only. The new mathematical progress remains internal finite-prefix LP analysis.
