./logs/iter_018_ideas.stderr.log:2869:Iteration 14 found no direct external theorem proving gluing or a separator. The internal progress is an exact separated-block value, an exact dual boundary identity, and a finite-alphabet dual reduction. Fulkerson-Gross supports the interval-incidence vocabulary for the finite-alphabet formula, Renault 2014 and existing uniform-value sources reinforce the need for stability beyond scalar finite-prefix values, and pseudonorm/approachability and countably-infinite LP sources are possible formulation tools only.
