./logs/iter_017_idea_02_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:4357:Iteration 12 adds internal exact finite-prefix machinery for deterministic known exogenous paths: the marginal reduction, finite-prefix LP dual \(D_n(P)\), and fixed-envelope compactness criterion. Literature checks found no direct theorem for this delayed-fill characterization. Lagziel-Lehrer 2015 is relevant delayed-approachability background for future vector-deficit formulations; Bistritz et al. 2022 is relevant weighted-regret delayed-bandit background for horizon-weighted certificates; Xie-Zhu-Shishkin 2025 is adjacent pricing context. All three should be cited as background only.
./logs/iter_017_idea_02_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:4359:Iteration 13 found no external theorem proving \(D_n=o(n)\Rightarrow o(T)\), nor a known market-path separator from the fixed-envelope criterion. The added approachability and uniform-value sources are background for possible formulations and for gluing cautions. Current internal proof work should focus on the last-exceedance/finite-prefix dual structure rather than importing uniform-value theorems wholesale.
./logs/iter_017_idea_02_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:4361:Iteration 14 found no direct external theorem proving gluing or a separator. The internal progress is an exact separated-block value, an exact dual boundary identity, and a finite-alphabet dual reduction. Fulkerson-Gross supports the interval-incidence vocabulary for the finite-alphabet formula, Renault 2014 and existing uniform-value sources reinforce the need for stability beyond scalar finite-prefix values, and pseudonorm/approachability and countably-infinite LP sources are possible formulation tools only.
