./logs/iter_015_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:2431:- Renault (Journal of Dynamics and Games 2014), "General limit value in dynamic programming," is verified. It gives a total-boundedness criterion for uniform convergence of values under vanishing-impatience evaluations. Relevant as uniform-value/gluing background only; it is not a theorem about delayed market making or \(D_n\).
./logs/iter_015_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:2470:Iteration 12 adds internal exact finite-prefix machinery for deterministic known exogenous paths: the marginal reduction, finite-prefix LP dual \(D_n(P)\), and fixed-envelope compactness criterion. Literature checks found no direct theorem for this delayed-fill characterization. Lagziel-Lehrer 2015 is relevant delayed-approachability background for future vector-deficit formulations; Bistritz et al. 2022 is relevant weighted-regret delayed-bandit background for horizon-weighted certificates; Xie-Zhu-Shishkin 2025 is adjacent pricing context. All three should be cited as background only.
