./logs/iter_014_idea_02_explorer_01.stdout.log:137:The strongest obstruction to a proof is conceptual: \(D_n=o(n)\) gives a new finite-prefix optimizer for each \(n\), while the fixed-envelope criterion requires one projectively consistent sequence. The finite-alphabet laminar structure may remove the abstract parity obstruction, but this remains unproved.
