./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3176:- Bistritz, Zhou, Chen, Bambos, and Blanchet (JMLR 2022), "No Weighted-Regret Learning in Adversarial Bandits with Delays," is verified. It studies delayed adversarial bandits with weighted-regret objectives and bounds involving total delay; relevant background for horizon-weighted finite-prefix dual certificates, not a delayed-fill characterization theorem.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3225:- Lagziel and Lehrer (Journal of Economic Theory 2015), "Approachability with delayed information," is verified. It gives delayed-information approachability/no-regret background and is relevant to vector-deficit formulations of simultaneous-horizon constraints; it does not prove the known-path finite-prefix LP or compactness criterion.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3238:- Bernstein and Shimkin (JMLR 2015) is verified. Response-based approachability may be algorithmically relevant if finite-prefix dual constraints are recast as vector-deficit feasibility; no direct delayed-fill result.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3239:- Dann, Mansour, Mohri, Schneider, and Sivan (COLT/PMLR 2025) is verified. It discusses rate-preserving reductions between approachability and generalized regret; relevant background for any future approachability formulation, not proof support for \(D_n\)-gluing.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3242:- Renault (Journal of Dynamics and Games 2014), "General limit value in dynamic programming," is verified. It gives a total-boundedness criterion for uniform convergence of values under vanishing-impatience evaluations. Relevant as uniform-value/gluing background only; it is not a theorem about delayed market making or \(D_n\).
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3287:Iteration 12 adds internal exact finite-prefix machinery for deterministic known exogenous paths: the marginal reduction, finite-prefix LP dual \(D_n(P)\), and fixed-envelope compactness criterion. Literature checks found no direct theorem for this delayed-fill characterization. Lagziel-Lehrer 2015 is relevant delayed-approachability background for future vector-deficit formulations; Bistritz et al. 2022 is relevant weighted-regret delayed-bandit background for horizon-weighted certificates; Xie-Zhu-Shishkin 2025 is adjacent pricing context. All three should be cited as background only.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3289:Iteration 13 found no external theorem proving \(D_n=o(n)\Rightarrow o(T)\), nor a known market-path separator from the fixed-envelope criterion. The added approachability and uniform-value sources are background for possible formulations and for gluing cautions. Current internal proof work should focus on the last-exceedance/finite-prefix dual structure rather than importing uniform-value theorems wholesale.
./logs/iter_016_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:3291:Iteration 14 found no direct external theorem proving gluing or a separator. The internal progress is an exact separated-block value, an exact dual boundary identity, and a finite-alphabet dual reduction. Fulkerson-Gross supports the interval-incidence vocabulary for the finite-alphabet formula, Renault 2014 and existing uniform-value sources reinforce the need for stability beyond scalar finite-prefix values, and pseudonorm/approachability and countably-infinite LP sources are possible formulation tools only.
